OAUTH2_PROXY_PROVIDER_DISPLAY_NAME=Authentik
OAUTH2_PROXY_CLIENT_ID=atheniq-portal
OAUTH2_PROXY_CLIENT_SECRET=REPLACE_ME
OAUTH2_PROXY_COOKIE_SECRET=REPLACE_ME
# When proxy's /data bind mount is not present (npm custom_ssl/nginx proxy_host
# configs, letsencrypt-acme-challenge, database.sqlite, keys.json), oauth2-proxy
# startup can still pass its own readiness checks but the estate cannot prove the
# proxy host is reachable through npm the way LMS conferral routing expects.
# Where oauth2-proxy is colocated with npm on the same host, the same /data bind
# mount that roots npm's proxy_host upstream is the bind mount oauth2-proxy must
# survive a remount without dropping live connections. If proxy's /data is missing
# (check-container-addresses.py reports the proxy by name with (/data not present)),
# this file alone is not the root cause — fix the container raw.mount first.
